From: Thomas Roos <thomas@roosesweb.de>
Subject: [PATCH] setup.py: don't require pkg_resources for requirements.txt parsing

Recent setuptools no longer ships pkg_resources. This only used
pkg_resources.parse_requirements() to turn requirements.txt lines into
requirement strings, which plain line parsing does just as well.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [project is unmaintained]
Signed-off-by: Thomas Roos <thomas@roosesweb.de>
---
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -1,12 +1,12 @@
 import pathlib

-import pkg_resources
 from setuptools import setup

 with pathlib.Path("requirements.txt").open() as requirements_txt:
     install_requires = [
-        str(requirement)
-        for requirement in pkg_resources.parse_requirements(requirements_txt)
+        line.strip()
+        for line in requirements_txt
+        if line.strip() and not line.strip().startswith("#")
     ]

 setup(
